<%# The phone navigation (structural redesign spec §4.3): four destinations, shown below 720px by
    shell.css. Lit by ShellHelper#sidebar_current, the same answer as the sidebar.

    THE FIFTH TAB IS "MORE" (UX audit A1): below 720px the rail is display:none, and it held the only
    way to Settings, Account, Trash, Inventory, Help, the theme and Sign out. More is a `details.menu`
    (menu_controller.js closes it on an outside tap and on Escape, returning focus to the summary)
    whose list opens upward as a sheet above the bar (shell.css). Its links come from
    ShellHelper#tabbar_more_links; the theme choice is the Settings page's own partial, so the two
    cannot disagree; Sign out is the rail's form. The tab lights through CSS when one of its links
    carries aria-current, so `sidebar_current` stays the one answer. A summary, not an `<a>`: it is
    not a place, and the four `a.tabbar-link`s stay the four places the tests count. %>
<nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Main">
  <% tabbar_links.each do |label, path, icon, lit| %>
    <%= link_to path, class: "tabbar-link", "aria-current": (lit ? "page" : nil) do %>
      <%= rail_icon(icon) %><span><%= label %></span>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <details class="menu tabbar-more" data-controller="menu">
    <summary class="tabbar-link"><%= rail_icon(:more) %><span>More</span></summary>
    <div class="menu-list tabbar-sheet">
      <% tabbar_more_links.each do |label, path, icon, lit| %>
        <%= link_to path, class: "menu-item", "aria-current": (lit ? "page" : nil) do %>
          <%= rail_icon(icon) %><span><%= label %></span>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      <div class="menu-sep" role="separator"></div>
      <div class="tabbar-theme">
        <span class="tabbar-sheet-label">Theme</span>
        <%= render "settings/theme" %>
      </div>
      <div class="menu-sep" role="separator"></div>
      <p class="tabbar-sheet-user" title="<%= current_user.email %>"><%= current_user.email %></p>
      <%= button_to destroy_user_session_path, method: :delete, class: "menu-item" do %>
        <%= rail_icon(:sign_out) %><span>Sign out</span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </details>
</nav>
